  "scenario": "A federal agency must transition its internal secure communications (VPNs, email, and document signing) to PQC. They use a mix of hardware (Cisco routers with RSA-4096) and software (Microsoft Exchange with ECDSA). The agency is mandated by executive order to use only NIST-standardized algorithms (FIPS 203, 204, 205) by 2030. They have a budget of $2,000,000 and a change freeze from Nov 15 to Jan 15. The agency's technical team has zero PQC experience, and the Cisco routers do not support firmware upgrades for PQC. The Microsoft Exchange servers will require a software update from Microsoft, which has not yet released a PQC plugin. The agency's cryptographic inventory is outdated and incomplete.",
